course: dictionary
lesson: 4105
title: Give and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word give has many meanings, so read the words around it to find the right one. Its meaning often depends on the small word that comes after it.
explain: «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.» Given away means handed out to other people, so fewer pencils are left for you.
explain: Give joins with small words to make new meanings: give up means stop trying, give in means stop arguing and let the other side win, and give way means let others go first. Check the small word before you decide.
fact: Give means to let someone have something, or to pass it to them.
fact: «Give us a go» (UK, Australia) means let me have a turn.
fact: «Give or take» means about, more or less.
fact: «Donate» is a more formal word for give, as in giving money to help.
fact: As a noun, give means stretch, as in «the rope has some give».
exercise: «A charity is a group that helps people or animals; to donate is to give money to help.» What does give mean in this sentence? | *To hand over money to help | To bend or break | To shout loudly | To stretch like a rope
exercise: «If 6 of those 24 pencils are given away, 24 − 6 = 18 are left.» What does given away mean? | Left behind on a bus | Made of wood | Counted twice | *Handed to other people, so they are no longer yours
exercise: Mia says, «I'll never finish this puzzle, I give up.» What does give up mean? | Stretch it as far as it will go | *Stop trying | Give a present to a friend | Start again from the beginning
test: At the sign, the driver must give way to the bus. What does give way mean? | Fall down | *Let others go first | Hand out sweets | Sing loudly
test: The walk took 20 minutes, give or take. What does give or take mean? | Exactly 20 minutes | Taking nothing at all | Given back to the walker | *About, more or less
exam: The exam says, «Given that the box is empty, we know it has no pencils.» What does given that mean? | We gave the box away | The box was a present for us | *We know that | Only if it is empty
